From 84a857c74af440e858f158f5e2754f77acc1a030 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:53:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-18: WPF Delete / Copy / Cut / Paste of whole
 components (0.18.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Like the WPF designer changing the XAML: the whole element (start tag through
its end tag -- or the <span style="position:absolute"> around an input) is
cut out of / put into the page source as ONE WorkspaceEdit (one Ctrl+Z), and
the designer draws the page again from the new source.
- Del (design surface, or the component tree): removed. When the page's JS
  uses the name (getElementById('x'), '#x' ...), a modal question first lists
  where (e.g. spbSave: ht9045_hotplate_wire.js:249, ht9045_wire_engine.js:2076);
  afterwards the parent is selected.
- Ctrl+C: the selected elements' HTML (multi-selection too), also on the
  system clipboard as text.
- Ctrl+V: a new copy -- every id renamed so none collides (spbSave ->
  spbSave_2, children too, the generated title="name : TClass" and
  <label for> with them); into the selected TPanel / TGroupBox (its
  <div class="cli">) / TTabSheet / the form, else next to the selected
  element; 8 px down-right on the page it came from; selected afterwards.
- Ctrl+X: copy, then delete (asks like Delete).
- Right-click menu (first group): 剪下 / 複製 / 貼上 / 刪除.
- Ctrl+C / X / V arrive as clipboard events (VS Code runs its clipboard
  commands inside the webview); one of a kind per 300 ms, so a doubled
  event can never paste twice.
- lib/htmlblock.js: elementRange, unitOf, renameIds, offsetBlock, insideEnd,
  removeRange (a pasted block deleted again leaves the page byte-identical).

Tests: lib 111, probe (Del / copy / paste -> commands, a doubled paste once),
smoke 72 (copy, paste + offset + one edit, delete asks and names the script,
delete of the copy = byte-identical page, paste into Panel2, cut), panels,
real VS Code 76 (paste drawn + selected, delete byte-identical, confirmed
delete of spbSave, Ctrl+Z brings it back, nothing saved) -- all pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
